<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"big-picture">Big p=
icture<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/latest/getting-started/kuber=
netes/self-managed-onprem/onpremises#big-picture" class=3D"hash-link" aria-=
label=3D"Direct link to Big picture" title=3D"Direct link to Big picture" t=
ranslate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<p>Install Calico to provide both networking and network policy for self-ma=
naged on-premises deployments.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"value">Value<a hre=
f=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/latest/getting-started/kubernetes/self-m=
anaged-onprem/onpremises#value" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct li=
nk to Value" title=3D"Direct link to Value" translate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a><=
/h2>
<p><strong>Calico networking</strong> and <strong>network policy</strong> a=
re a powerful choice for a CaaS implementation. If you have the networking =
infrastructure and resources to manage Kubernetes on-premises, installing t=
he full Calico product provides the most customization and control.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"concepts">Concepts=
<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/latest/getting-started/kubernetes/=
self-managed-onprem/onpremises#concepts" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"=
Direct link to Concepts" title=3D"Direct link to Concepts" translate=3D"no"=
>=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"recommended-tigera=
-operator">Recommended: Tigera Operator<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/ca=
lico/latest/getting-started/kubernetes/self-managed-onprem/onpremises#recom=
mended-tigera-operator" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Re=
commended: Tigera Operator" title=3D"Direct link to Recommended: Tigera Ope=
rator" translate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>Calico is installed by an operator which manages the installation, upgra=
de, and general lifecycle of a Calico cluster. The operator is
installed directly on the cluster as a Deployment, and is configured throug=
h one or more custom Kubernetes API resources.</p>
<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"calico-manifests">=
Calico manifests<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/latest/getting-sta=
rted/kubernetes/self-managed-onprem/onpremises#calico-manifests" class=3D"h=
ash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Calico manifests" title=3D"Direct li=
nk to Calico manifests" translate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>Calico can also be installed using raw manifests as an alternative to th=
e operator. The manifests contain the necessary resources for installing Ca=
lico on each node in your Kubernetes cluster. Using manifests is not recomm=
ended as they cannot automatically manage the lifecycle of the Calico as th=
e operator does. However, manifests may be useful for clusters that require=
 highly specific modifications to the underlying Kubernetes resources.</p>
